    "body": "Closes #86.\n\nReverts the custom HTML parser added in #87, following ADR-006.\n\n## Why\n\nAfter implementing and testing the custom parser and a GTK-based renderer, we found that the approach conflicts with ADR-001, which states we should:\n\n- Use `lexbor` for HTML parsing\n- Use `Cairo + Pango` for rendering\n- Write the layout engine in-house\n\nGTK is a widget toolkit, not a rendering engine. Using it to render HTML leads to workarounds that multiply with each new feature.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Adds `docs/decisions/006-return-to-adr-001.md` documenting the decision\n- Marks ADR-004 as superseded by ADR-006\n- Deletes `src/renderer/html/` (node.hpp, parser.hpp, parser.cpp)\n- Deletes `tests/test_parser.cpp`\n- Reverts `src/CMakeLists.txt` (removes parser.cpp from honeybee_lib)\n- Reverts `tests/CMakeLists.txt` (removes test_parser.cpp)\n\n## Preserved\n\nThe custom parser and renderer are preserved on the branch `feat/html-renderer` for future reference and educational value.\n\n## Next\n\nWith this PR merged, main returns to the state of PR #87 (all work after that — the GTK renderer — is dropped). The next step is to import lexbor and build a real DOM layer on top of it.",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-03T05:45:33Z",
